{"title":"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be an irrational number with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b616f2cf1d5626ca6e70dd3804c7288d4addf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\alpha &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"13\" />, and draw a circle in the plane whose circumference has length 1.  Given any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, define a sequence of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> as follows.  First select any point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> on the circle, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc5ae30a4bbf51ae529e0d2fbdbdf4b07798930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\le k \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" /> define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebaba4ae3d5c911d6e31ad855d502ad88d48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> as the point on the circle for which the length of arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90d27f75e568c161aa1065b29d0b9ce18bc933b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{k - 1} P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, when travelling counterclockwise around the circle from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f11ab8936ec43ea50c80ca2c67a1b4d2fe6ab34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{k - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebaba4ae3d5c911d6e31ad855d502ad88d48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />.  Supose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d874e17c7ea25b97dc858c88374b891b2a6f6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/15245bc6e388de68e6fa07b00f49b5386c770d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> are the nearest adjacent points on either side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/130f017b31ab3b50b451b177eebcaf0b8b85bdd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Use mathematical induction. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> it is true because one point can't be closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9090f2e6bd5da465fea10a8c755d64e9185f61f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> in both ways, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/8/1b8857cc5dba4aae2c106e3240b3f5b4ca6019cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2\\le 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />. Suppose that for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the nearest adjacent points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d874e17c7ea25b97dc858c88374b891b2a6f6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/15245bc6e388de68e6fa07b00f49b5386c770d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> on either side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> satisfy  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201c65d7f8dff3e04e7eeca0eb76d184c36908ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. Then consider the nearest adjacent points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe288e3048ab6eaa4dd26fe6b67f9a8ccc7ebfc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/74505c8c90cbac5d5ca5e984a5dbb0be2d3f2535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> on either side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c898e4838db56320e10a77c62839f4237c974733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />. It is by the assumption of the nearness we can see that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be0d03ba61547ca6ab19c1f555bfa9a3a74b0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c,d)=(a+1,b+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" /> still holds, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> jumps into the interior of the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/4931ffda6a5c361c27c337b41a374a855b13f4f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{a+1}P_{n}P_{b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equals to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let's consider the following two cases.\n</p><p>(i) Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e42302f9dd0afe4a7cd50ac2115f72bee849423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since the length of the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/13478ee6e54d332a7c9de87471ce3d361a36d143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_nP_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c901d5c70aa0c82bda136f6a7ae09ab8bdd016b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{(a-n)\\alpha\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df2919191b1220773d9b0142dec5c3528fd4c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> equals to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> subtracted by the greatest integer not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />) and length of the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/3980c67a9221a9ad69a9bf42a9c5818d6aadf30b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_bP_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aab0c293fcafb65b4d9f6fc6dd9dc80c9a2cccd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{(n-b)\\alpha\\} = \\{a\\alpha\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />, we now consider a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> which is defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> traveling clockwise on the circle such that the length of arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f87574947eecd302ba2d136ae87aa3b03b81f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. We claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> is in the interior of the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5ad839084efe7f1954112f6fc918ccf7bcd417c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_bP_nP_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />. Algebraically, it is equivalent to either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/4875a3cc7a1c6808be8e688e3a3652b3f10cddca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0-n\\alpha\\} &lt; \\{a\\alpha-n\\alpha\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/3/2c3410356d14aa06289a73e716e56b7d473b043a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{n\\alpha -0 \\} &lt; \\{n\\alpha - b\\alpha\\} = \\{a\\alpha\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose the latter fails, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/41426ff5c8d324f8272ab4d02ca4495020fe1e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{n\\alpha\\} \\ge \\{a\\alpha\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />. Then suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ff973f7a82bec1fd679602f90d66e59e320d3ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\alpha = m_1 + r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2fb813991bab9505d6228e8c1c3f2da8180ec6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\alpha = m_2 + r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d659c8074c617549d61db9db0773e0fccad7b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee54e8432d4a60984309e86f32931b04c8e2f1da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> are integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/e/99ea4904f987a5de0167997646bb2e826c2c4b2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt; r_2\\le r_1 &lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is not zero because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/5/e95707f4c7d91cfb011359fa85640d7282614645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\alpha$\" width=\"20\" height=\"8\" /> is irrational). We now have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8e8dd06db4dc4cc224271f0fd239c6d391f896a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{0-n\\alpha\\} = \\{-m_1-1 + (1 -r_1)\\}=1-r_1\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f5e9b169973c63fd07b3ed1666f4b1f85247e31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{a\\alpha -n\\alpha\\} = \\{m_2-m_1-1 + (1+r_2-r_1)\\} = 1+r_2-r_1&gt;1-r_1\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> is either closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d874e17c7ea25b97dc858c88374b891b2a6f6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d874e17c7ea25b97dc858c88374b891b2a6f6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> side, or closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/15245bc6e388de68e6fa07b00f49b5386c770d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/15245bc6e388de68e6fa07b00f49b5386c770d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> side. In other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> is the closest adjacent point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c898e4838db56320e10a77c62839f4237c974733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1defd9edc2aea91bb1972250a100e7f689930219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{a+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> side, or the closest adjacent point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c898e4838db56320e10a77c62839f4237c974733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f9db86b20caa4da1d59ada53d3ad27be2717ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" /> side. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe288e3048ab6eaa4dd26fe6b67f9a8ccc7ebfc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/74505c8c90cbac5d5ca5e984a5dbb0be2d3f2535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbf2158f412866ad063799935600f03eab2f094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d \\le n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>(ii) Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b7ddd96e1f845c2828b485707f07498c5ac400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\le n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />\nThen either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20afc34400f879415e5698a2622d18f31d0c0c37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d = (a+1)+(b+1) \\le n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"259\" height=\"18\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f806621f2494eb9f42f4be9b6d78d06e3b0bb0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/980e769452bc4c032c309fc642c4c231e6bf2d18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f74ab72b4c061b4ffc8c5d71aa1e33cb5aa8b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d \\le 1+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> when one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe288e3048ab6eaa4dd26fe6b67f9a8ccc7ebfc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/74505c8c90cbac5d5ca5e984a5dbb0be2d3f2535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>In either case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/289cc0565c97b2a3314447f5502f10ec1cc12638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d\\le n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> is true.\n</p><p>--<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Lightest\" title=\"User:Lightest\">Lightest</a> 20:27, 6 May 2012 (EDT)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\">USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO\" title=\"2012 USAJMO\">2012 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=